<!--
 This file contains a list of the ADKs which will be pulled from maven as a 
 part of the build.  The '<dependency>...</dependency>' constructs list the
 actual ADKs.

 We also use different configurations if we want a jar file to be downloaded
 to a different directory.  These configurations are invoked from the
 main build.xml file.  

 When specifying a configuration for a dependency it is of the format:
    <configuration-name>-><type> (e.g. general->master).

 The <type> is usually one of two:
   1. general - which means that the dependency, and all files which it is
                dependent upon is retrieved;
   2. master  - which means that only the specified file is retrieved (i.e. no
                additional dependencies will be retrieved).

-->

